@flexiarg operator/fill-the-wait-with-bounded-work
@title Fill the Wait with Bounded Work
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-7moxqm turn-YRKf71; first proposed for: A wait has just been declared with a known trigger and rough duration (the restart deferred to a pause point, 'maybe in an hour').
@why [apparatus/every-wait-has-a-deadline]

! conclusion: Slot a bounded, interruptible piece of work into the window ('until then we could run the sweep'), sized to the wait's stated bound.

  + IF:
    There is work available that fits the window and does not contend for the busy resource.

  + HOWEVER:
    An unfilled wait is dead time; but filling it with open-ended work risks overrunning the trigger and colliding with the thing being waited for.

  + THEN:
    Slot a bounded, interruptible piece of work into the window ('until then we could run the sweep'), sized to the wait's stated bound.

  + BECAUSE:
    Every-wait-has-a-deadline makes the wait's extent knowable; this proposal exploits that knowability — only because the wait has a trigger and a bound can the window be safely filled with work.
